{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463370",
      "title": "Vue Reactivity: A Deep Dive",
      "lectureOrder": 63,
      "videoOrder": 56,
      "sourceHash": "44aaff86fc1ac62638fd2cd4c8eef2e89e04c7d7ca7af0f3dce1454f9f10e6e5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.05,
          "end": 4.207,
          "en": "For a second, I will leave Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.207,
          "end": 6.83,
          "en": "to dive into that proxy thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.83,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "which is built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 10.88,
          "en": "which Vue uses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.88,
          "end": 13.69,
          "en": "And let's leave the Vue world here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.69,
          "end": 15.85,
          "en": "and write some vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.85,
          "end": 17.53,
          "en": "We have a variable message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.53,
          "end": 18.87,
          "en": "where I say Hello!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.87,
          "end": 21.71,
          "en": "So this is a regular JavaScript variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.71,
          "end": 24.13,
          "en": "It has nothing to do with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.13,
          "end": 26.38,
          "en": "Now, the interesting thing about JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.38,
          "end": 30.363,
          "en": "is that if I now have a new longMessage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.17,
          "end": 34.24,
          "en": "which is my old message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.24,
          "end": 36.83,
          "en": "plus let's say World,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.83,
          "end": 40.21,
          "en": "I can, of course, console.log that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.21,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "and we would see Hello! World!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 46.27,
          "en": "If I save that, open the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.27,
          "end": 49.39,
          "en": "and reload, we see Hello! World! here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.39,
          "end": 52.01,
          "en": "Now that shouldn't be too surprising.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.01,
          "end": 54.58,
          "en": "But now if we change message thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.44,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "to Hello and a couple of exclamation marks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 64.96,
          "en": "if I console.log longMessage again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.96,
          "end": 67.9,
          "en": "and I reload, I still get Hello, World!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.9,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "I don't get all these exclamation marks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 75.25,
          "en": "Instead, I just have one exclamation mark after Hello!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.25,
          "end": 80.18,
          "en": "Because JavaScript by default is not reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.18,
          "end": 81.8,
          "en": "That is really just something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.8,
          "end": 83.99,
          "en": "which Vue adds for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.99,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "JavaScript by default is not reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 90.23,
          "en": "If we have a calculation, like we have it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.23,
          "end": 92.09,
          "en": "where we use a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.09,
          "end": 94.64,
          "en": "and we change that variable thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.64,
          "end": 96.71000000000001,
          "en": "that calculation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.71000000000001,
          "end": 98.53,
          "en": "is not re-executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.53,
          "end": 101.7,
          "en": "JavaScript doesn't note that message changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.7,
          "end": 103.483,
          "en": "and that it was used here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.5,
          "end": 107.67,
          "en": "So that is how JavaScript works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.67,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "and Vue works differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 111.68,
          "en": "Vue has a built-in mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.68,
          "end": 114.38,
          "en": "to be aware when message changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.38,
          "end": 115.84,
          "en": "so that parts of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 115.84,
          "end": 118.85,
          "en": "that rely on message can be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.85,
          "end": 121.87,
          "en": "And as mentioned for that, it uses proxies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.87,
          "end": 124.723,
          "en": "So let's see how proxies could work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.86,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "For that, let me remove that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 131.07,
          "en": "and let's create an object, data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.07,
          "end": 133.15,
          "en": "which is just an empty JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.15,
          "end": 135.22,
          "en": "again not related to Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.22,
          "end": 138.03300000000002,
          "en": "And let's put the message in here, Hello!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.23,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "Now we can wrap this object with a proxy in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 147.56,
          "en": "by creating a new Proxy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.56,
          "end": 150.3,
          "en": "And that is a constructor function built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 152.5,
          "en": "into modern JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.5,
          "end": 154.67000000000002,
          "en": "Therefore, make sure you're testing this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.67000000000002,
          "end": 157.09300000000002,
          "en": "in a modern browser like Chrome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.15,
          "end": 161.16,
          "en": "Now, we can store that proxy in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 161.16,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "and this proxy wants the object it should wrap.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 166.94,
          "en": "In this case, data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.94,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "But it does not just want this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 173.3,
          "en": "Instead, it wants a second object as a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.3,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "and that will be an object full of handlers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 179.12,
          "en": "for that wrapped object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.12,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "Now, I'll come back to what that is in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 185.53,
          "en": "Let's first of all create such a handler object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.53,
          "end": 189.78,
          "en": "This handler object can now use certain features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.78,
          "end": 192.72,
          "en": "It can set up so-called traps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.72,
          "end": 194.92,
          "en": "which proxies support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.92,
          "end": 198.53,
          "en": "For example, set traps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.53,
          "end": 201.28,
          "en": "You do this by adding a set function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.28,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "in the handler and as a argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 207.963,
          "en": "you will automatically receive a target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 211.343,
          "en": "a key and a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.7,
          "end": 214.7,
          "en": "Now, to understand what this does,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.7,
          "end": 217.543,
          "en": "let's console.log target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.523,
          "end": 224.223,
          "en": "key and value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.39,
          "end": 227.9,
          "en": "And let's now pass this handler object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.9,
          "end": 231.96,
          "en": "as a second argument to our proxy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.96,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "Now, it's said that the proxy would wrap this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.11,
          "en": "this data object, the first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.11,
          "end": 238.72,
          "en": "and indeed it does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.72,
          "end": 243.11,
          "en": "So on the proxy, we can indeed access message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.11,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "just as if we would have a message property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 248.37,
          "en": "on the created proxy object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.37,
          "end": 249.96,
          "en": "because actually, we will.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.96,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "It wraps this data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 253.58,
          "en": "This object has a message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.58,
          "end": 255.623,
          "en": "So the proxy also has one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.61,
          "end": 258.14,
          "en": "And we can set this to Hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.14,
          "end": 260.7,
          "en": "with a couple of exclamation marks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "Now, let's save and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "and what you should see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.96,
          "en": "is that you get three console.log messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.96,
          "end": 270.28,
          "en": "because we have three console.logs here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.28,
          "end": 274.33,
          "en": "The first one, the target is essentially the object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 274.33,
          "end": 276.31,
          "en": "that was wrapped here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.31,
          "end": 278.93,
          "en": "That's just your object that was wrapped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278.93,
          "end": 281.59000000000003,
          "en": "The second one, the key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.59000000000003,
          "end": 286.35,
          "en": "is the property that you just set a new value to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.35,
          "end": 288.8,
          "en": "And the third one, the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.8,
          "end": 290.85,
          "en": "is the value that was set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 290.85,
          "end": 292.37,
          "en": "And that hopefully shows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 292.37,
          "end": 294.14,
          "en": "what a handler does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 294.14,
          "end": 297.74,
          "en": "With that, we can define a setter function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 297.74,
          "end": 302.72,
          "en": "which is triggered whenever a property is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 302.72,
          "end": 305.52,
          "en": "to a new value on this proxy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 308.64,
          "en": "and then we can find out which property that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 308.64,
          "end": 310.35,
          "en": "what the new value is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.35,
          "end": 312.943,
          "en": "and which original object we wrapped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.18,
          "end": 319.18,
          "en": "And we could then use this if we had another property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.31,
          "end": 321.12,
          "en": "Let's say a longMessage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 321.12,
          "end": 323.663,
          "en": "which initially is Hello! World!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 324.64,
          "end": 327.88,
          "en": "But we want to ensure that longMessage changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 327.88,
          "end": 329.63,
          "en": "if message changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 329.63,
          "end": 331.453,
          "en": "Let's say that's our goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 332.78,
          "end": 334.68,
          "en": "Now, by using a proxy,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 334.68,
          "end": 339.06,
          "en": "and setting up such a handler with a so-called set trap,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.06,
          "end": 340.63,
          "en": "we can implement this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 340.63,
          "end": 343.93,
          "en": "We can check if the key we're setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 343.93,
          "end": 348.93,
          "en": "is message, so if we're setting the message property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 350.46,
          "end": 352.25,
          "en": "and if we do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.25,
          "end": 353.78,
          "en": "we want to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 356.11,
          "end": 357.97,
          "en": "target.longMessage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.35,
          "end": 365.35,
          "en": "equal to the new value we assigned for message, plus World!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 367.93,
          "end": 369.8,
          "en": "And thereafter, we also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 369.8,
          "end": 372.13,
          "en": "that the message property itself is set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 372.13,
          "end": 375.793,
          "en": "so we set target.message equal to value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 377.2,
          "end": 379.68,
          "en": "And the interesting thing can now be seen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 379.68,
          "end": 384.46,
          "en": "if we console.log proxy.longMessage thereafter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.46,
          "end": 387.97,
          "en": "at the end after setting the message to Hello",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.97,
          "end": 389.76,
          "en": "with multiple exclamation marks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 389.76,
          "end": 392.94,
          "en": "and after updating our handler here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.94,
          "end": 394.15999999999997,
          "en": "If we now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 394.15999999999997,
          "end": 398.06,
          "en": "we see that down there from line 40,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 398.06,
          "end": 399.72,
          "en": "we're outputting the longMessage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 399.72,
          "end": 403.899,
          "en": "which now picks up all those extra exclamation marks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 403.899,
          "end": 407.61,
          "en": "So longMessage was updated when we set message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 407.61,
          "end": 411.1,
          "en": "So here we built our own reactive system",
